# Resolve from the public registry regardless of the machine's npm config.
#
# `package-lock.json` records a `resolved` URL per package, so whichever
# registry the developer who last ran `npm install` happened to be pointed at
# is the one baked into the lock — and a company mirror baked in here is a
# host CI (and everyone else) cannot reach: `npm ci` hangs, then dies with
# "Exit handler never called!", and the build fails on modules that are simply
# not there. Pinning the registry for this package keeps the lock portable.
registry=https://registry.npmjs.org/
